cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OMNIS — Observational Minimal-length Nonparametric Inductive Synthesis"
message: "If you use OMNIS in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Silva
    given-names: Jorge Miguel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6331-6091"
    affiliation: "IEETA / DETI, University of Aveiro, Portugal"
abstract: >-
  OMNIS is an empirical Solomonoff inductor for integer sequences. Given a
  target sequence, it searches for the shortest register-machine program that
  reproduces it exactly under a canonical instruction set, ranked by Minimum
  Description Length. A candidate counts as a discovery only when it both
  compresses the training data and predicts a held-out continuation exactly.
keywords:
  - solomonoff-induction
  - minimum-description-length
  - program-synthesis
  - inductive-synthesis
  - integer-sequences
  - oeis
  - kolmogorov-complexity
